+		 * NOTHING — that is the whole contract, because a reader uses it to decide whether the
+		 * gauges it just read all came from one generation. Refreshing here would destroy the
+		 * only thing a reader can use to detect a mixed tuple, so this case deliberately sits
+		 * ahead of the fallback: 0 ("no snapshot has ever been taken") is a truthful answer. */
+		return snap->sequence;
